.TH MINSEC-SYNC.TOML 5 "" "minsec" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
minsec-sync.toml \- minsec multiplayer client configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/minsec/sync.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
This TOML file configures
.BR minsec-sync (1).
Its existence is the packaged service's multiplayer opt-in switch.
When it is absent,
.B minsec-sync run
exits successfully without enrollment, network access, key creation, reporting,
or firewall changes.
Other subcommands treat an absent file as an error.
.PP
Every key is optional and has a default.
An empty file therefore opts in with all standard behavior enabled.
Unknown keys are errors.
Unlike the daemon configuration, this file has no drop-in directory and no
table sections.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BI server " = URL"
Base URL for enrollment, report, and feed endpoints.
The value must begin with
.B http://
or
.BR https:// .
Production deployments should use HTTPS.
Trailing slashes are ignored.
Default:
.IR https://api.minsec.io .
.TP
.BI tier " = \(dqbasic\(dq | \(dqhigh\(dq"
Crowd-feed tier.
.B basic
uses the basic feed policy;
.B high
selects the stricter high-confidence feed.
Default:
.BR basic .
.TP
.BI report " = boolean"
When true,
.B minsec-sync run
submits new automatic local bans.
This flag does not disable an explicitly invoked
.B minsec-sync report
command.
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.BI pull " = boolean"
When true,
.B minsec-sync run
fetches and applies crowd feeds.
This flag does not disable an explicitly invoked
.B minsec-sync pull
command.
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.BI ipv4 " = boolean"
Fetch and maintain the IPv4
.B crowd4
set during a pull.
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.BI ipv6 " = boolean"
Fetch and maintain the IPv6
.B crowd6
set during a pull.
Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.BI state_dir " = path"
Directory containing the private signing key and client state.
It is created when needed.
Default:
.IR /var/lib/minsec/sync .
.TP
.BI events " = path"
Daemon JSON Lines event log read by the report operation.
Only automatic ban records are submitted.
Default:
.IR /var/lib/minsec/events.jsonl .
.TP
.BI nft " = path-or-command"
nftables executable used to manage crowd sets.
The value is executed directly, not through a shell.
Default:
.BR nft .
.SH REPORTING AND PRIVACY
Reporting reads complete, newline-terminated automatic ban events beyond the
saved inode and byte-offset cursor.
It submits the attacker network, event timestamp, filter/category, hit count,
and ban lifetime.
It does not submit log text, usernames, or local user data.
Manual bans are skipped.
.PP
IPv4 reports must be /24 or narrower.
IPv6 reports must be /48 or narrower; networks narrower than /64, including
host /128s, are aggregated to /64.
Events older than approximately 23 hours, implausibly future events, malformed
networks, and invalid filter names are skipped.
.SH STATE AND FIREWALL
The state directory contains
.B key
(a 32-byte Ed25519 signing seed created with mode 0600) and
.B state.json
(enrollment, event, sequence, and feed cursors).
State updates use a temporary file followed by rename.
Protect this directory and preserve it across upgrades.
.PP
Pull operations manage only the
.B crowd4
and
.B crowd6
sets in
.BR "table inet minsec" .
Setting
.B ipv4
or
.B ipv6
to false stops updates for that family but does not flush existing elements.
Setting
.B pull
to false has the same persistence property.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
server = "https://api.minsec.io"
tier = "basic"
report = true
pull = true
ipv4 = true
ipv6 = true
state_dir = "/var/lib/minsec/sync"
events = "/var/lib/minsec/events.jsonl"
nft = "nft"
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/minsec/sync.toml
Configuration and opt-in marker.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/minsec/sync.toml.example
Packaged example with default values and opt-out guidance.
.TP
.I /var/lib/minsec/sync/key
Default private signing-key path.
.TP
.I /var/lib/minsec/sync/state.json
Default client-state path.
.TP
.I /var/lib/minsec/events.jsonl
Default event-log input.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR minsec-sync (1),
.BR minsec (1),
.BR minsec.toml (5),
.BR nft (8)
